# Agent Game Review — example environment configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     python3 -m agr review <run_id> --provider openai
#
# The CLI auto-loads `./.env` at startup via python-dotenv (bundled with the
# `.[model-anthropic]` / `.[model-openai]` extras that `agr review` needs anyway;
# override the path with `--env-file`). A real session/OS environment variable
# always takes precedence over the file, so exporting a key still wins.
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. The deterministic pipeline (ingest / show / eval /
# serve) needs no credentials at all — these only matter for the Stage F model
# reviewer (`agr review`). Never commit your real `.env` (it is gitignored).

# --- Which model the reviewer uses -------------------------------------------
# Resolves as: `--model` flag  >  AGR_REVIEW_MODEL  >  the provider's default.
# Set the id for whichever --provider you run (anthropic | openai-compatible).
# AGR_REVIEW_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# AGR_REVIEW_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.1-70b-instruct

# --- Anthropic model reviewer (`--provider anthropic`) -----------------------
# Used by `pip install .[model-anthropic]` + `agr review --provider anthropic`.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: point the Anthropic SDK at a compatible gateway instead of the
# default api.anthropic.com. Same effect as `--base-url` for that provider.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# --- OpenAI-compatible model reviewer (`--provider openai`) ------------------
# Used by `pip install .[model-openai]` + `agr review --provider openai`.
# Works against ANY OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so you can use any model.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional endpoint override (same as `--base-url`). Point at OpenRouter,
# Together, Groq, or a local vLLM / Ollama / LM Studio server. For a local
# server that ignores auth, still set OPENAI_API_KEY to any non-empty value.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# --- Contract confirmation (`agr confirm`) -----------------------------------
# Optional identity recorded as the confirming reviewer. Falls back to the OS
# user (USER / USERNAME / LOGNAME) when unset.
# AGR_CONFIRMED_BY=
